  "notes": "Composed of {印|いん} (print, stamp) + {字|じ} (character, letter). Refers specifically to the printing of text characters, as opposed to images or graphics. Commonly used in business and manufacturing contexts for labels, receipts, and documents.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {印字|いんじ}する — to print (characters)\n- {印字|いんじ}が{薄|うす}い — the print is faint\n- {印字|いんじ}{品質|ひんしつ} — print quality\n- {印字|いんじ}{速度|そくど} — print speed\n- {印字|いんじ}{面|めん} — printed surface\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {印刷|いんさつ} — printing; broader term covering all types of printing, including images and mass production\n- プリント — print; loanword used for printing in general\n- {刻印|こくいん} — engraving, stamping; physically pressing characters into a surface",
